            <description><![CDATA[<h2>RestinPID 3.4</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Needs Attention:</b> apps that aren’t responding, and busy macOS apps, now gather in one group at the top of the list so you see them first. Prefer them at the bottom? Settings → Apps.</li>
<li><b>Cleaner rows:</b> the “Not Responding” badge sits next to the app’s name, and RAM and CPU always stay on one line.</li>
<li><b>Fewer false alarms:</b> an app is marked “Not Responding” only after it misses two checks in a row, so a single slow moment no longer flags it.</li>
<li>The arrow keys move through the list in the order you see it.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
